        {
          "question": "e-5839",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "A reciprocal function is defined for all values of $x$ except those that make the denominator zero. To find the domain, we must exclude all values of $x$ that make the denominator zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-x & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is  $x \\in (-\\infty,2) \\cup (2 ,\\infty).$",
