      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5841",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{a}{bx+c} + d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\in (-\\infty, d)\\cup (d,\\infty).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d = 2.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y = 2,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\in (-\\infty, 2) \\cup (2, \\infty).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078796/assets/fb344a1c6613805bab7bcc04c8b711b5ba1c26eef36197c45b03205e2bc5dbc6.png)",
